// Expected: §4.17 "The element names `pre` and `code` … are raw-content elements … the block splitter SHALL
//           scan the body as a single text run terminated only by the matching close tag" — the text renders.
// Actual:   exit 1 `error [E-TYPE-026]: `match` is not valid directly in markup (§18.9). Wrap the match in a
//           logic interpolation — e.g. `${ match subject { .A => <p>a</> else => <p>b</> } }` …` (stage TS).
//           The raw body reached the typer's markup-match check. (The message also still teaches `=>` arms.)
<program>
<pre>
match @phase {
  .Idle :> "idle"
}
</pre>
</program>
